        "date": "2026-11-27T19:42:18Z"
      },
      "message": "test(examples): add the wrapped A-axis catalog case\n\nAdd examples/catalog/multiaxis/wrapped: a 20 mm bar along X with a\nround-bottom ring groove. Rotary Offset roughs it, Rotary Parallel\nfinishes it and its end faces, and Rotary Contour cuts rings over the\ngroove, on the Tormach 770MX + microARC 4 with the Tormach PathPilot\npost. Each posted operation turns A.\n\nThe held pin moves into the example_catalog directory suite. The full\nregenerate and rebuild checks are in the heavy lane (about 30 s each in\ndebug alone). The guide pages of the three kinds link the case.\n\nA groove that wanders along X is refused by the rotary kinds (#2772).\nWithout a setup the post refuses a B word (#4422).\n\nFixes #2869\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "25524c804a23708c74843ffbb2e1ea247c59409e",
